  "img": "systems/draw-steel/assets/classes/conduit.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are a <strong>vessel for a power on the other side of the Veil</strong> - a believer with a pact, channeling the aid of an angel across the Veil into the prime world through sheer conviction. Your power flows from <strong>Conviction</strong>: the measure of your standing with your patron, spent to call aid. The corp records call it a <em>pastoral-services contractor</em>; the street calls you the <strong>Street-Priest</strong>, a padre, a collar, a saint.</p><p>Your engine is <strong>Conviction</strong>: a steady per-turn drip (+2 at the start of each of your turns), with an optional <strong>prayer gamble</strong> layered on top - spend your maneuver to pray instead of taking the flat drip, then roll 1d6 for a chance at more. The first time each round you heal or protect an ally, you bank a <strong>creed echo</strong> (+1). You spend Conviction on heroic abilities, on Spend X enhancement riders, and on invoking the pact. Unspent Conviction is lost at the end of the encounter.</p><h3>Signatures &amp; Subclass</h3><p>Three signatures cost no Conviction: <strong>Lay On Hands</strong> (spend a Recovery to heal), <strong>Smite/Rebuke</strong> (your core attack, a Presence Power Roll), and <strong>Sense the Veil</strong> (read spirits, souls, and corruption). At Tier 5 you choose a subclass ministry - Shepherd, Templar, or Exorcist - that colors your signatures and grants an identity feature.</p><h3>Kit &amp; Chrome</h3><p>A light-Kit class. Foci over chrome: reliquaries, blessed symbols, consecrated censers, warded vestments, bought with nuyen. Chrome is strongly discouraged - a soul cluttered with chrome is a poor vessel, and the Street-Priest guards their Body Integrity to keep the pact open.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass ministry, gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic ability. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability and your Conviction cap rises. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
